    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "In the previous chapter, we created linked lists where each node directly points to the next node, and the last node points to nullptr. This type of linked list is known as a singly linked list."
    },
    {
      "type": "image",
      "alt": "Singly Linked List",
      "src": "data:image/png;base64,"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Now, we'll make linked lists where the last node points back to the head node. This kind of linked list is called a circular linked list."
    },
    {
      "type": "image",
      "alt": "Circular Linked List",
      "src": "data:image/png;base64,"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Here, the last node points to the head node, creating a circular structure."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Now that we know what circular linked lists are, let's see why we need them."
    },
